The Comedy of Hello and World, in Which Nobody Dies For Once.

Romeo, a young man with a fine ear for arithmetic and none at all for romance.
Juliet, a lady who speaks in single letters, and only when she is told.


                    Act I: A Greeting, Assembled By Hand.

                    Scene I: Romeo Counts Out The Letters Of A Hello.

[Enter Romeo and Juliet]

Romeo:
 You are as noble as the sum of a fine fair sweet golden mighty noble rose and a
 brave bold fine hero. Speak your mind!

Romeo:
 You are as golden as the sum of yourself and a fine fair sweet golden mighty
 rose. You are as fair as the difference between yourself and a fine hero. You
 are as sweet as the difference between yourself and a rose. Speak your mind!

Romeo:
 You are as mighty as the sum of yourself and a brave bold fine hero. You are as
 proud as the difference between yourself and a rose. Speak your mind! Remember
 yourself. Remember yourself.

Romeo:
 Recall the letter thou hast twice set aside. Speak your mind!

Romeo:
 You are as brave as the sum of yourself and a brave fine hero. You are as bold
 as the difference between yourself and a rose. Speak your mind! Remember
 yourself.


                    Scene II: A Comma, And A Breath.

Romeo:
 You are as sorry as the difference between yourself and a fine fair sweet
 golden mighty noble rose. You are as bad as the difference between yourself and
 a fine hero. You are as horrid as the difference between yourself and a rose.
 Speak your mind!

Romeo:
 You are as vile as the difference between yourself and a brave bold fine hero.
 You are as foul as the difference between yourself and a brave fine hero. Speak
 your mind!


                    Scene III: And Now The World, Which Is Further Off.

Romeo:
 You are as amazing as the sum of yourself and a fine fair sweet golden mighty
 noble rose. You are as cursed as the difference between yourself and a brave
 bold fine hero. You are as dirty as the difference between yourself and a rose.
 Speak your mind!

Romeo:
 Recall the round letter thou art keeping. Speak your mind!

Romeo:
 You are as handsome as the sum of yourself and a brave fine hero. You are as
 stuffed as the difference between yourself and a rose. Speak your mind!

Romeo:
 Recall thy last remembered letter. Speak your mind!

Romeo:
 You are as smelly as the difference between yourself and a brave bold fine
 hero. Speak your mind!

Romeo:
 You are as damned as the difference between yourself and a fine fair sweet
 golden mighty noble rose. You are as stupid as the difference between yourself
 and a fine hero. You are as rotten as the difference between yourself and a
 rose. Speak your mind!

Romeo:
 You are as small as the sum of a brave bold fine hero and a fine hero. Speak
 your mind!

[Exeunt]
